+"	SGA45-CORR-0002;S45-ASTRA-A-0003;S45-ASTRA-A-0002	insert	1	0	1	108	AI-translated: newly supplied or restored English prose	New translation of restored authorial prose		plain toc chapter A thread of Ariadne for SGA SGA and SGA A thread of Ariadne for SGA SGA and SGA Exposés I to VI of SGA give the general theory of Grothendieck topologies Very detailed they can be valuable when studying exotic topologies such as the one that gives rise to crystalline cohomology For the étale topology so close to classical intuition such an imposing safeguard is unnecessary it suffices to know for example Godement's book and to have a little faith Other possible references are Chapters I to III of Artin's notes Giraud's Bourbaki exposé or Arcata I Exposés VII and VIII begin the study of the étale topology They are more detailed than Chapter III of Artin and Arcata II The study of curves is the key to étale cohomology Artin begins it in Exposé IX of SGA consequences concerning cohomological dimension are given in X The essential points are taken up in Arcata III Exposé XI is unnecessary for what follows it contains an elegant proof of the comparison theorem between étale cohomology and classical cohomology in the special case of smooth complex algebraic varieties Exposés XII and XIII prove the fundamental base change theorem for a proper morphism As Artin observed in algebraic approximation of structures over complete local rings Publ Math IHES pp his approximation theorem makes it possible to simplify the proof This is the route followed in Arcata IV where the many dévissages in the proof are only sketched and the applications in Exposé XIV are indicated only very briefly The theorem makes it possible to define cohomology with compact supports and the higher direct image with proper supports functors whose properties reduce to those of the higher direct image functors for a proper morphism This is the subject of the prolix Exposé XVII the essentials are given in Arcata IV but portions of XVII may be independently useful Exposés XV and XVI centre on the fundamental local acyclicity theorem for smooth morphisms The influence of SGA shows through in the less detailed parallel exposé Arcata V which also contains the proof of the results needed from SGA The exposé Arcata VI is devoted to Poincaré duality it is clearer than SGA XVIII but does not claim to give a complete proof For those who insist on a purely algebraic proof it is simplified by a reference to Duality it does not contain the proof of the formalism obeyed by the trace morphism XVIII In étale cohomology there is a duality formalism analogous to that of coherent cohomology To establish it Grothendieck used resolution of singularities and the purity conjecture for the statement see Cycle established in a relative setting in SGA XVI and modulo resolution in equal characteristic in SGA XIX The key points are established by another method in Finiteness th for schemes of finite type over a regular scheme of dimension or Various developments are given in SGA I In SGA III it is shown how this formalism implies the very general Lefschetz Verdier trace formula We see that in the original version of SGA the Lefschetz Verdier formula was established only conjecturally Moreover its local terms were not calculated For the application to functions this seminar contains another proof this one complete in the special case of the Frobenius morphism This is the one that appears in Report Other references for the statement and the outline of the dévissages Grothendieck's Bourbaki exposé for a brief description of the reduction due to Grothendieck of the crucial case to a case already treated by Weil for an adic treatment of this last case Cycle SGA also contains a detailed treatment of the passage from cohomology to cohomology Exposés V and VI by J P Jouanolou and of the formalism of the Frobenius morphism Exposé XV by C Houzel Exposés X and XIII written by I Bucur calculate the Euler Poincaré characteristic of a sheaf on a curve and the trace of the endomorphism of its cohomology defined by certain correspondences In VII Jouanolou calculates the cohomology of classical schemes and gives applications Furthermore Serre's exposé Introduction à la théorie de Brauer was included in his book Part Bibliography M Artin Grothendieck topologies Harvard University P Deligne les constantes des équations fonctionnelles des fonctions In Modular functions of one variable II pp Lecture Notes in Math Springer Verlag J Giraud Analysis situs Séminaire Bourbaki May Benjamin R Godement Topologie algébrique et théorie des faisceaux Act Sci et Ind Hermann A Grothendieck Formule de Lefschetz et rationalité des fonctions Séminaire Bourbaki Dec Benjamin J P Serre Représentations linéaires des groupes finis Collection Méthodes Hermann SGA Séminaire de Géométrie algébrique du Bois Marie SGA Théorie des topos et cohomologie étale des schémas directed by M Artin A Grothendieck and J L Verdier Lecture Notes and SGA Cohomologie adique et fonctions directed by A Grothendieck to appear in Lecture Notes	Reviewed-page association, not an assertion that every listed decision caused every token in this hunk.	component	source/en/release_v2026-11-12/05_SGA4HALF_EN_COMPLETE_READER.tex	deliverables/EN/SGA4HALF_EN_corrected_apparatus.tex#component-ariane	Every equal and changed opcode reconstructs this complete comparison unit exactly. Corrected variant branches are selected. opening.tex and toc-i.tex are expanded when the supplied French component includes them; original local bibliographies and contents are included. Decision IDs are page associations unless explicitly present in the hunk.
